#-- nanosoc_iice_debug.prj -- Synplify Premier project carrying an Identify
#-- (IICE) implementation for the MPS3 nanoSoC DFX reconfigurable module.
#--
#-- =====================================================================
#-- STATUS: NEVER EXECUTED. Not by Synplify, not by identify_debugger, and
#-- never against hardware. Authored 2026-07-29 from
#-- docs/planning/IDENTIFY_IICE_DFX_PLAN.md and the one working reference in
#-- reach: HAPS-work/HAPS-SX/examples/hello_ident/build/hello_ident.prj.
#-- Treat every value below as a proposal to be checked on first run.
#-- =====================================================================
#--
#-- WHICH COPY IS AUTHORITATIVE
#--   The SYNTHESIS project lives with the RM build (fpga/rp/nanosoc_iice/**,
#--   owned elsewhere). The debugger must open the project the *build* produced,
#--   because it refuses to load without `rev_1_identify/syn.db` and reads the
#--   IICE description from that implementation's `identify.db`
#--   (hello_ident/README.md, "Files the debugger needs"). This file is the
#--   host-side reference of what that project must contain, and the fallback to
#--   copy into a build directory if you are debugging a bitstream whose project
#--   was not archived. Point debug_session.tcl at whichever copy is real:
#--       IICE_PRJ=/path/to/build/nanosoc_iice_debug.prj \
#--           identify_debugger_shell host/identify/debug_session.tcl
#--
#-- WHY AN "identify"-TYPE IMPLEMENTATION
#--   `impl -add rev_1_identify -type identify` + `set_option
#--   -identify_debug_mode 1` is what makes plain batch synthesis run
#--   identify_db_generator + identify_compile and weave the IICE in. The
#--   instrumentation is read from rev_1_identify/identify.idc, seeded from the
#--   generated .idc (tests/identify_iice/build/<IICE>.idc). Do NOT script
#--   identify_instrumentor_shell -- in 2022.09 `project open` silently kills
#--   script execution (hello_ident/README.md:28-30).

#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-- RTL. Placeholder only: the real source set is 226 files / 77,637 lines,
#-- flattened from $SOCLABS_NANOSOC_SOC_DIR/pynq/filelist.tcl plus 5 repo-side
#-- files (IDENTIFY_IICE_DFX_PLAN.md §5 Phase 3). The RM build owns that list
#-- and must emit it here in dependency order, PACKAGES BEFORE CONSUMERS.
#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# add_file -verilog -vlog_std sysv "<generated file list goes here>"
add_file -fpga_constraint "./nanosoc_iice.fdc"

#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-- Implementation: Identify type. The name `rev_1_identify` is not cosmetic --
#-- it is the directory the debugger looks in.
#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
impl -add rev_1_identify -type identify

#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-- Device. XCKU115-FLVB1760, speed grade -1, commercial: the MPS3's part is
#-- `xcku115-flvb1760-1-c` (fpga/monolithic/README.md:16, 272/272 PACKAGE_PINs
#-- validated against the real package DB). Part + package + grade are all
#-- CONFIRMED present in
#--   /eda/.../SFPGA_2022.09-SP2/fpga/lib/parts/xilinx_parts.txt:1687-1702
#-- which lists XCKU115 with package FLVB1760 and grade -1-c.
#--
#-- -technology IS UNVERIFIED. xilinx_parts.txt groups XCKU115 under
#-- `target Kintex-UltraScale-FPGAs`, and xilinx_families.info (which maps
#-- targets to mapper families) is encrypted, so the token Synplify expects
#-- could not be read. `KINTEXU` is the conventional Synplify spelling; if
#-- synthesis rejects it, try the target name verbatim:
#--     set_option -technology "Kintex-UltraScale-FPGAs"
#-- and record which one worked. (hello_ident used the board alias
#-- HAPS-SX-VU19P-32G, which is no guide for a bare part.)
#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
set_option -technology KINTEXU
set_option -part XCKU115
set_option -package FLVB1760
set_option -speed_grade -1
set_option -part_companion ""

#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-- Compilation / mapping.
#--
#--   -top_module        The RM boundary module. If plan risk R1 turns out to be
#--                      real -- `device jtagport soft` adding the four
#--                      identify_jtag_* ports to the top -- the Synplify top
#--                      becomes a thin shim that carries exactly the 35 contract
#--                      ports (docs/contracts/partition-pins.md) and ties
#--                      identify_jtag_{tck,tms,tdi,tdo} to swd_{clk,dio_o,
#--                      dio_oe,dio_i}. Change this line, not the contract.
#--   -disable_io_insertion 1
#--                      MANDATORY here, for two independent reasons: the
#--                      OOC/EDIF handoff into the DFX flow needs pad-less
#--                      ports, and `jtagport soft` needs its four ports to stay
#--                      pad-less too (plan §2).
#--   -identify_debug_mode 1
#--                      Turns on the Identify jobs in batch.
#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
set_option -top_module "rp_nanosoc_wrapper"
set_option -disable_io_insertion 1
set_option -identify_debug_mode 1
set_option -write_vif 1

#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-- Result. The EDIF basename MUST be exactly <top_module>.edf or Vivado's
#-- link_design fails with "[Project 1-68] No files found to match top module"
#-- (plan §7, first trap). Case sensitive.
#-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------
project -result_file "./rev_1_identify/rp_nanosoc_wrapper.edf"

impl -active "rev_1_identify"
